2","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $4.2M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $995K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $153K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Opendoor Technologies Inc is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.1B market cap on $4.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -35% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -557% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 8% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 17.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 5.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 29% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 67/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Real Estate peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 97% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 134% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"These Metro Detroit restaurants are open on Thanksgiving Day 2026","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/metro-detroit-restaurants-open-thanksgiving-110525000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482309.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"This Fort Worth restaurant news is stuffed with closures and openings","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/fort-worth-restaurant-news-stuffed-234206000.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794615833.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"These 4 Travel Stocks Depend on Holiday Spending","source":"aol.com","link":"htt